  "verdict": "tune-open: t16 family measures 0 divergent bits vs legacy (bounds <7e-6) and 15-45% faster per launch; pack8_gemv_decode re-confirmed non-bit-exact at the control rate and stays rejected",
  "evidence_note": "The timing screen alone observed 0 legacy-vs-candidate bit diffs, which is underpowered for the known ~1e-4 divergence rate of the rejected rewrite (expected <1 diff per shape sample); the 200-trial rate screen corrects that: the rejected control reproduces ~9e-5 on every shape while t16_gemv_decode and t16_gemv_decode_rowtile4 report 0/422400..0/1638400. Timings are 3-run medians on an idle GPU1; per-launch device cost only (no queue/host effects). Wiring t16 needs a tile-storage decision: the byte-neutral repack is not the raw layout prefill kernels read, so a routed tensor needs either both layouts or a tile-reading prefill consumer."
